# Building an Authoring Interface

*Learn how to create a visual configuration UI for your PIE element.*

## Overview

The authoring interface (often called "configure") lets authors visually build questions using your element. While optional, a good authoring UI makes your element much more accessible.

## Coming Soon

This tutorial will cover:

### 1. The Configure Component

```javascript
import React from 'react';

export default class Configure extends React.Component {
  render() {
    const { model, configuration, onModelChanged, onConfigurationChanged } = this.props;

    return (
      <div>
        {/* Your authoring UI here */}
      </div>
    );
  }
}
```

### 2. Core Authoring Patterns

**Prompt Editor**:
```javascript
<EditableHtml
  markup={model.prompt}
  onChange={(prompt) => onModelChanged({ ...model, prompt })}
  imageSupport={configuration.imageSupport}
/>
```

**Choice Management**:
```javascript
<ChoiceEditor
  choices={model.choices}
  correctResponse={model.correctResponse}
  onChoicesChanged={(choices) => onModelChanged({ ...model, choices })}
  onCorrectResponseChanged={(correctResponse) =>
    onModelChanged({ ...model, correctResponse })
  }
/>
```

**Settings Panel**:
```javascript
<Tabs>
  <Tab label="Design">
    {/* Main editing UI */}
  </Tab>
  <Tab label="Scoring">
    {/* Scoring configuration */}
  </Tab>
  <Tab label="Settings">
    {/* Advanced options */}
  </Tab>
</Tabs>
```

### 3. Using pie-lib Components

PIE provides reusable authoring components:

```javascript
import {
  EditableHtml,
  Collapsible,
  FeedbackConfig,
  InputContainer
} from '@pie-lib/pie-toolbox/config-ui';

// Use in your configure component
<FeedbackConfig
  feedback={model.feedback}
  onChange={(feedback) => onModelChanged({ ...model, feedback })}
/>
```

### 4. Live Preview

Show authors what students will see:

```javascript
import MyElement from '../element';

<div className="preview">
  <h3>Student View</h3>
  <MyElement
    model={studentModel}
    session={{ value: null }}
  />
</div>
```

### 5. Validation & Feedback

```javascript
class Configure extends React.Component {
  validate() {
    const errors = [];

    if (!this.props.model.prompt) {
      errors.push('Prompt is required');
    }

    if (!this.props.model.correctResponse) {
      errors.push('Must specify correct answer');
    }

    return errors;
  }

  render() {
    const errors = this.validate();

    return (
      <div>
        {errors.length > 0 && (
          <Alert type="error">
            <ul>
              {errors.map(e => <li key={e}>{e}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </Alert>
        )}
        {/* Rest of UI */}
      </div>
    );
  }
}
```

### 6. Advanced Features

**Drag & Drop**:
```javascript
import { DragDropContext, Droppable, Draggable } from 'react-beautiful-dnd';

// Reorderable choices
```

**Rich Media Upload**:
```javascript
import { ImageUpload } from '@pie-lib/pie-toolbox/config-ui';

<ImageUpload
  onUpload={(url) => onModelChanged({ ...model, imageUrl: url })}
/>
```

**Templates**:
```javascript
const templates = [
  { name: 'Basic', model: { /* ... */ } },
  { name: 'With Images', model: { /* ... */ } },
];

<TemplateSelector
  templates={templates}
  onSelect={(template) => onModelChanged(template.model)}
/>
```

### 7. Package Configuration

```json
{
  "name": "@pie-element/my-element",
  "pie": {
    "element": "@pie-element/my-element",
    "configure": {
      "tag": "my-element-configure"
    }
  }
}
```

